1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,160
So we've come up seething lane into hart street.
我们沿Seething Lane走到Hart Street。

2
00:00:06,160 --> 00:00:16,241
And looking here to the right you can see the gardens and the church of crited friers with all the kitchen garden the convent garden.
看右边，地图上能看到那座教堂和花园，还有菜园、修道院花园；教堂名在字幕中识别不稳定。

3
00:00:16,241 --> 00:00:20,720
And that would have sat along to the right of the frame here.
那些地方原本就在画面右边这一带。

4
00:00:22,521 --> 00:00:26,681
Which is fascinating isn't it and one of the things I'm interested in looking for today.
很有意思，对吧？我今天感兴趣、想找的一件事是……

5
00:00:26,681 --> 00:00:33,120
If there's any kind of markers or remnants of even buildings that would have gone.
看看有没有某种标记、残迹，哪怕建筑本身已经消失。

6
00:00:33,120 --> 00:00:38,120
Is there something still here like the main gate there I wonder what's at the site of the main gate.
这里还留着什么吗？比如主入口，我想知道主入口原址上如今有什么。

7
00:00:38,120 --> 00:00:50,000
A crutched frier pub there on the other side of the road from the frery itself.
那边有一家Crutched Friar酒吧，就在原修道院马路对面；修道院相关词被识别为frery。

8
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:54,640
This is basically the site of crutched friers.
这里基本就是那座修道院的原址。

9
00:00:54,640 --> 00:01:01,150
Now here's the name of kja french ordinary cord opposite crutched fries.
这里有一个名字，字幕作kja、French Ordinary Cord，就在Crutched Friars对面；这些专名待听辨复核。

10
00:01:01,160 --> 00:01:10,481
And there is a place here on the map a little alleyway there that leads into the the mana of blanch appleton.
地图上有这样一个地方，一条小巷通向字幕作mana of blanch appleton的旧庄园；专名待核。

11
00:01:10,481 --> 00:01:19,361
I feel like I have to go that way what's that over there just uh behind the railway bridge.
我觉得非得往那里走一趟。那边是什么？就在铁路桥后面。

12
00:01:19,361 --> 00:01:24,921
It's interesting I'm seeing things I've never never noticed before even though I've walked around here recently making a video that's the thing isn't it.
有意思，我注意到一些以前从没发现的东西，虽然最近才来这里走过、拍过视频；就是这么回事，对吧？

13
00:01:24,921 --> 00:01:32,241
When you engage in these processes it opens up new perspectives on the city.
参与这样的过程，会让你对城市产生新的看法。

14
00:01:32,241 --> 00:01:40,921
This is a classic kind of psycho geographical technique for a duie is to take an out ofd map or an old map of places that no longer exist.
这是一种经典的心理地理漫步技巧：拿着过时的地图，或一张标有已消失地点的旧地图；技巧名字幕作duie，待核。

15
00:01:40,921 --> 00:01:51,351
And walk that city it's one of the the classics that I think the situationist international used to do in paris in the 50 s and 60 s.
然后走进那座城市。我想，这是情境主义国际在五六十年代巴黎常做的事情之一。

16
00:01:51,361 --> 00:01:58,080
So yeah it's great and and you know we'll discover things that have nothing to do with chudah london.
所以很棒，而且我们会发现一些和都铎伦敦毫无关系的东西。

17
00:01:58,080 --> 00:02:05,681
Look at this street here so this is um savage gardens which I walked I started to walk up the bottom end of this.
看看这条街。这是Savage Gardens，我先前走过，开始沿它底部那一段走。

18
00:02:05,681 --> 00:02:09,721
But didn't realize it extended through here isn't this delightful.
但我没意识到它一直延伸到这里。这不是很令人愉快吗？

19
00:02:09,721 --> 00:02:16,760
And you've got some old kind of warehouse buildings here obviously definitely not chuda.
这里有一些老仓库建筑，显然肯定不是都铎时期的；字幕作chuda。

20
00:02:16,760 --> 00:02:28,681
But what's interesting is this curve in the road here you can see up ahead um is reflected in the 1520 map as well.
有意思的是，前面能看到的这处道路弯曲，在1520年的地图上也有体现。

21
00:02:28,681 --> 00:02:37,961
Except that on the 1520 map everything to the left there were gardens reaching as far as uh fenur street to the left.
只不过在1520年的图上，左边全是花园，一直延伸到字幕所说的fenur street。

22
00:02:37,961 --> 00:02:47,921
So we're going to walk up to old gate and old gate street and come back along furch street and pick up some of those other buildings.
我们走到字幕作old gate和old gate street的地方，再沿furch street回来，看看其他一些建筑；街名待核。

23
00:02:47,921 --> 00:02:56,520
The population of london in 1520 was 50 000 which made it the biggest city in England and one of the biggest cities in Europe.
据他的讲述，1520年伦敦人口为五万，使它成为英格兰最大、欧洲最大城市之一。

24
00:02:56,520 --> 00:02:57,520
If not the world.
他补充说，甚至可能是当时世界最大的城市之一。

25
00:02:57,520 --> 00:03:09,671
But it's an interesting moment in time to reconstruct london at 1520 because a number of things were about to happen which radically reshaped the city itself.
但选择1520年来复原伦敦很有意思，因为接下来会发生几件事，彻底改变城市本身。

26
00:03:09,681 --> 00:03:19,031
1520 so Henry vii had been on the throne for 11 years he was still probably happily married to katherine of aragan.
在1520年，国王已在位十一年，可能仍和凯瑟琳维持幸福婚姻；字幕henry vii和aragan可能误识，待原声核对。

27
00:03:19,041 --> 00:03:25,760
Thomas cromwell was about to move into his mansion at austin friar.
托马斯·克伦威尔即将搬进Austin Friar的宅邸；地点拼写待核。

28
00:03:25,760 --> 00:03:31,561
No idea that he'd end up at the scaffold at tower hill yeah 20 years later.
当时他不会知道，二十年后会在Tower Hill走向刑台，嗯。

29
00:03:31,561 --> 00:03:39,671
But this city on the map here looks radically different by 1600 or by certainly by the victorian period.
但地图上的城市，到1600年，或者说至少到维多利亚时代，已经显得截然不同。

30
00:03:39,681 --> 00:03:48,200
There was a population explosion which meant that by 1600 just 80 years later the population of london was 200 000.
据他说，人口迅速增长，到1600年，仅八十年后，伦敦人口达到二十万。

31
00:03:48,200 --> 00:03:53,760
Not just london in the city but also it broke out into the suburbs into the fields around the city.
不只是城内的伦敦，城市还向郊区和周围田地扩展。

32
00:03:53,760 --> 00:03:56,921
One of the factors there was the dissolution of the monasteries.
其中一个因素，据他的讲述，是修道院的解散。

33
00:03:56,921 --> 00:04:08,041
So on the map all that kind of pink shades of pink land that belong to monastic buildings naries various other church buildings a lot of that.
地图上那些深浅粉红色的土地，属于修道院、字幕作naries的机构和其他教会建筑，其中很大一部分……

34
00:04:08,041 --> 00:04:12,760
The monasteries were dissolved much of that building uh went into private hands.
修道院解散后，许多建筑转入私人手中。

35
00:04:12,760 --> 00:04:17,880
Pass the crown and the crowd sold them often to wealthy courtiers who did very well out of it.
先经过王室，再出售，常卖给富有的宫廷人士，他们从中获得很大利益；原字幕pass/crowd疑有误识。

36
00:04:17,880 --> 00:04:24,080
Because they managed to get that property in the in the 15 th 30 s 1540 s before the population explosion hit.
因为他们在1530年代、1540年代，人口激增之前，就已经买到这些房产。

37
00:04:24,080 --> 00:04:27,681
And that value of that property absolutely boomed.
那些房产的价值随后大幅上涨。

38
00:04:27,681 --> 00:04:37,031
Some of the monastic buildings became simple churches and we've been walking around the city churches haven't we as well and seeing that some of them predate this 1520 map.
有些修道院建筑变成普通教堂。我们也一直在看城里的教堂，对吧？其中一些比这张1520年地图还早。

39
00:04:37,041 --> 00:04:40,520
But all those bits of pink would suddenly look quite different.
但所有那些粉红色区域会突然呈现出很不一样的面貌。

40
00:04:40,520 --> 00:04:47,241
Of course every one of those churches or monasteries naries they had gardens and courtyards and open spaces.
当然，每一座这样的教堂、修道院，以及字幕作naries的机构，都有花园、庭院和开阔空间。
